  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0215 database is designed to manage information related to airline operations, including passenger details, flight schedules, aircraft information, and luggage handling. The Passenger table stores details about individuals who have booked flights, with each passenger assigned a unique AccountID, which is used to link them to their ticket and luggage information. The Passenger table also includes the passenger's name, age, and frequent flyer ID. The Airport table contains information about the airports served by the airline, with each airport identified by a unique AirportCode, which is used to link airports to flights and aircraft. The Aircraft table stores details about the planes used by the airline, including the AirplaneNumber, make, weight limit, and flight number, which is linked to the Flight table. The FlightCrew table holds information about the airline's employees, including their EmployeeID, name, title, age, and address, with the AirportCode linking them to the airport where they are based. The Flight table contains details about each flight, including the flight number, departure and arrival times, price, airport code, gate number, and the employee ID of the pilot, which links them to the FlightCrew table. The Ticket table stores information about each ticket sold, including the ticket ID, from and to locations, seat number, price, flight status, class, and the AccountID of the passenger who booked the ticket, which links to the Passenger table. The Luggage table stores information about each piece of luggage, including the LuggageID, carousel number, weight, and the AccountID of the passenger who checked the luggage, which links to the Passenger table, as well as the AirplaneNumber, which links to the Aircraft table.",
  "gold_question": "American Airlines Operations Application\n\n1) Background / Context\nAmerican Airlines requires a comprehensive application to support their day-to-day operations. The system is intended to manage critical data related to passengers, airport activities, aircraft, flight crew, and flight logistics using a MySQL database.\n\n2) Objectives\n- To streamline management of flight operations, crew, and ticketing.\n- To enhance data accessibility and management for operational efficiency.\n- To integrate diverse operational components within a unified system.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n- Airline Operations Managers\n- Flight Crew Members\n- Ticketing Agents\n- Passengers\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n- Manage passenger information, including account details and frequent flyer data.\n- Maintain airport details, including codes, names, and locations.\n- Track aircraft details such as make, weight limits, and assigned flight numbers.\n- Handle flight crew details including personal information and assigned airport.\n- Schedule and manage flight information including departure, arrival times, and pricing.\n- Issue tickets with route specifics, seating, pricing, and flight status.\n- Transport luggage management, correlating with passenger and flight details.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n- Ensure data integrity and referential integrity across all entities.\n- Support efficient data retrieval to handle operational demands.\n- Maintain system security for sensitive data related to flights and passengers.\n- Achieve high availability and reliability to support continuous airline operations.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0215.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0215\nCREATE TABLE `passenger` (\n  `account_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `age` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `frequent_flyer_id` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`account_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `airport` (\n  `airport_code` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`airport_code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `aircraft` (\n  `airplane_number` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `make` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `weight_limit` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`airplane_number`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `flight_crew` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `age` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `airport_code` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `flight_crew_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`airport_code`) REFERENCES `airport` (`airport_code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `flight` (\n  `flight_number` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `departure_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `arrival_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `airport_code` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `gate_number` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `pilot_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`flight_number`),\n  CONSTRAINT `flight_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`airport_code`) REFERENCES `airport` (`airport_code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `flight_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`pilot_id`) REFERENCES `flight_crew` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `ticket` (\n  `ticket_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `from_location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `to_location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `seat_number` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `flight_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `class` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `account_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`ticket_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `ticket_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`account_id`) REFERENCES `passenger` (`account_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `luggage` (\n  `luggage_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `carousel_number` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `weight` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `account_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `airplane_number` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`luggage_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `luggage_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`account_id`) REFERENCES `passenger` (`account_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `luggage_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`airplane_number`) REFERENCES `aircraft` (`airplane_number`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
